---
import ResourceLayout from '../../components/ResourceLayout.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
import InfographicViewer from '../../components/InfographicViewer.astro';
import ExternalResource from '../../components/ExternalResource.astro';
---

<ResourceLayout
  icon="💳"
  eyebrow="Insurance and healthcare costs"
  title="Health Coverage"
  introduction="Learn how provincial health insurance works, what services are covered, and how newcomers can access healthcare in British Columbia."
>
  <VideoEmbed
    title="Healthcare Coverage for Newcomers in British Columbia"
    videoId="CnZjlt38KVo"
    description="Watch this short video to learn about MSP, health insurance, and healthcare coverage available to newcomers in British Columbia."
  />

  <InfographicViewer
    title="Healthcare Guide for BC Newcomers"
    description="Learn how BC's healthcare system works, what Medical Services Plan (MSP) covers, and where to find additional support."
    previewSrc="/infographics/mental-health/Healthcare-Guide-for-BC-Newcomers-en.png"
    previewAlt="Preview of the Healthcare Guide for BC Newcomers infographic"
    languages={[
      {
        label: 'English',
        href: '/infographics/mental-health/Healthcare-Guide-for-BC-Newcomers-en.png',
        lang: 'en',
      },
      {
        label: 'ਪੰਜਾਬੀ',
        href: '/infographics/mental-health/Healthcare-Guide-for-BC-Newcomers-pa.png',
        lang: 'pa',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <ExternalResource
    icon="🇨🇦"
    source="Government of British Columbia"
    title="Medical Services Plan (MSP)"
    description="Learn who is eligible for BC's Medical Services Plan, what services are covered, and how to enroll."
    href="https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/health/health-drug-coverage/msp"
  />

  <section>
    <h2>Provincial health insurance</h2>
    <p>
      British Columbia's Medical Services Plan (MSP) helps pay for many medically
      necessary healthcare services. Most eligible residents should register for
      MSP as soon as possible after arriving in British Columbia.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is usually covered?</h2>
    <p>
      MSP generally covers medically necessary visits with physicians, hospital
      care, diagnostic tests, and many emergency services. Coverage for other
      healthcare services depends on the type of care and your circumstances.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What may not be fully covered?</h2>
    <p>
      Prescription medications outside the hospital, dental care, vision care,
      physiotherapy, counselling, ambulance services, and many medical devices
      may require additional insurance or out-of-pocket payment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Private health insurance</h2>
    <p>
      Many employers, schools, and private insurance plans help cover services
      that MSP does not fully pay for, including medications, dental treatment,
      eyeglasses, and counselling.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Newcomers and healthcare coverage</h2>
    <p>
      Eligibility for MSP depends on your immigration status and residency.
      Some newcomers may need temporary private health insurance until their
      provincial coverage begins.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Ask about costs before receiving care</h2>
    <p>
      If a service is not urgent, ask whether it is covered before your
      appointment. Clinics, pharmacies, settlement agencies, and insurers can
      help explain potential costs and available coverage.
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="notice">
    <strong>Do not delay emergency care.</strong>
    <p>
      If you are experiencing a medical emergency, call 911 or go to the nearest
      emergency department immediately. Questions about insurance or payment
      should never delay urgent medical treatment.
    </p>
  </aside>
</ResourceLayout>